my name is Liam Reeves I'm a cosplayer  and I've been doing this for the last 24  years today we are blowing a bell jar  for a reproduction of an early 18th  century vacuum pump initially we gather  the glass from the furnace using what's  called a blowing iron which is  essentially a stainless steel tube  and then we shape the glass using wooden  blocks and newspaper we soaked that in  water the the burning action of the  glass creates a carbon layer and then  the water in the newspaper turns into  steam and creates a cushioning layer so  you can shape the glass but because it's  malleable you can it's much more  versatile and you can use it to create  shapes and do lots of different things  the gloss blow then blows down the tube  to introduce air into the glass to  inflate here you use the air itself but  then usually in conjunction with  centrifugal force in gravity and other  shaping tools included in the newspaper  to create shapes and push the glass in  different directions in the middle of  the process I create a bottleneck on the  end of the bowl of the jar to do that I  use basically oversized steel tweezers  and you pinch the glass and then stretch  a neck part out  the glass cools down very rapidly so it  goes from being very liquid to being act  like solid you know I've quite a short  period of time so part of being a glass  barrier is being able to work the glass  in different ways at different stages so  glass playing is very much a two-person  activity you can do a certain amount on  your own but it really does need two  people clause playing essentially hasn't  really changed at all in a thousand  years it's essentially the same process  that it was then the only difference  really is that now we use electronic  controllers to measure of the  temperature and we use gas to fire the  furnace it's a it's a very difficult  craft to learn it takes six years to  learn the basics and twelve to be a  master it can be extremely frustrating  it can be punishingly hot at the same  time it's all extremely addictive it can  be very very good fun it can be very  satisfying it's all of those really  [Music]  [Music]
 

